&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance: &lt;/strong&gt;Cal. Lab. Code §432.3 (pay scale disclosure &amp;amp; salary history ban); Cal. Lab. Code §1197.5 (Equal Pay Act); Cal. Gov. Code §12940 (FEHA); 42 U.S.C. §2000e (Title VII); 29 U.S.C. §621 (ADEA); 42 U.S.C. §12101 (ADA)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;

a16z-zipline:greenhouse:7676378003.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Repair and Reliability Platform team builds the systems that preserve asset health and keep the delivery network operational as aircraft, infrastructure, and fleet complexity scale. We create software that detects issues in live operations, orchestrates maintenance and repair workflows, evaluates airworthiness, and helps technicians return constrained assets to service quickly and safely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team owns the operational backbone that connects fleet health, maintenance execution, technician operations, and return-to-service decisions into a single reliability platform. The systems we build directly influence aircraft availability, delivery capacity, operational safety, and the network’s ability to scale reliably.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own software in the critical path of fleet reliability and maintenance operations, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;fleet health and asset visibility systems that track the operational state of aircraft, infrastructure, and distributed site assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;maintenance orchestration platforms for issue management, work orders, technician workflows, and scheduled maintenance execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;airworthiness and configuration control systems that evaluate whether aircraft can safely return to service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;usage tracking and lifecycle systems that monitor component wear and drive preventative maintenance policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;operational tooling used by maintenance teams, service engineering, and flight operations to diagnose issues, coordinate interventions, and maintain fleet readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;reliability automation and event-driven systems that connect live operational signals to issue detection and repair workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hard problems, real ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most software roles optimize digital experiences. This role helps maintain and restore a live autonomous logistics network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on problems like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;maintaining trustworthy real-time visibility into fleet health across aircraft, infrastructure, and distributed operational sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;preventing avoidable downtime by detecting degradation before it impacts delivery operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;building systems that connect issue detection to fast, correct maintenance execution and return-to-service decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;designing operational tooling that helps technicians and operators make reliable decisions under time pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;evaluating airworthiness and maintenance policy compliance at fleet scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;managing maintenance workflows across a globally distributed network with evolving hardware configurations and operational constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These are production systems with immediate operational consequences. The software you build directly impacts fleet availability, operational safety, delivery capacity, and operator trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own critical parts of the platform end to end, make technical and product decisions, and shape how reliability systems scale across the network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team operates with high ownership, high trust, and a high technical bar. Engineers are expected to identify important operational problems, develop a clear point of view on how systems should behave, and drive solutions from concept through production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value engineers who combine strong systems thinking with operational empathy and who care deeply about building software operators and technicians can trust under real-world conditions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also expect engineers to use AI tooling effectively as a force multiplier across exploration, implementation, debugging, and operational analysis, while maintaining strong engineering rigor, judgment, and accountability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are likely a strong fit if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;have experience building reliable production systems in operationally complex environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;can turn ambiguous reliability and maintenance problems into durable software systems others depend on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;combine strong backend and systems engineering judgment with product instinct and operational awareness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;care deeply about correctness, reliability, safety, and operator trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;can simplify operational complexity and design abstractions that scale across fleets, assets, and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;thrive in environments where software, hardware, and operations are tightly coupled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;are comfortable owning systems with real-world consequences and high expectations for reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;want to shape architecture, operational workflows, and long-term platform direction, not just implement scoped features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is best suited to engineers who want to own critical operational systems, make consequential technical decisions, and help scale the reliability backbone of a real-world autonomous logistics network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Else You Need to Know&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting cash range for this role is $180,000- $270,000 base salary. Please note that this is a target starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. The final cash payment for this role will depend on various factors, including a specific candidate’s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may include equity compensation; discretionary annual or performance bonuses; sales incentives; benefits such as medical, dental, and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion or religious creed, mental or physical disability, medical condition, genetic information, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, military or veteran status, citizenship, or other characteristics protected by state, federal or local law or our other policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-zipline:greenhouse:7718629003.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Zipline&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest autonomous delivery system, built to provide fast, reliable access to medicine, food, and other essential goods. We design, build, and operate high-performance logistics systems that serve customers across healthcare, retail, and government on four continents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Manufacturing Engineering team builds the production systems that turn complex designs into reliable, scalable hardware. We are looking for engineers who like solving practical problems, moving quickly, and building equipment that works in the real world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You and the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Zipline, manufacturing capability is a core part of the product. We are looking for a highly capable Production Equipment &amp;amp; Tooling Design Engineer to join our Manufacturing Engineering team. In this role, you will design and deliver the custom production equipment, fixtures, jigs, workstations, assembly aids, and test tooling that enable safe, repeatable, and scalable builds across our aircraft, zips, docks, and critical feeder subassemblies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a deeply cross-functional role. You will work closely with design engineers, manufacturing engineers, quality engineers, operations program managers, technicians, maintenance teams, and external vendors to bring equipment from concept through commissioning and sustainment. You will own equipment and tooling projects end-to-end: defining requirements, generating concepts, building CAD, releasing detailed designs, supporting fabrication, debugging on the floor, validating performance, and driving continuous improvement after launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a hands-on mechanical designer with strong manufacturing instincts. You understand that great production equipment is not just functional—it is safe, ergonomic, robust, serviceable, and easy for operators and technicians to use. You move quickly, make sound engineering tradeoffs, and know how to turn ambiguity into practical hardware that improves throughput, quality, and cost.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design custom production tooling, fixtures, jigs, workstations, automated and semi-automated equipment for Drone, Delivery pod, Dock, Zipline Dropbox, Subassembly and other builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop detailed 3D CAD, drawings, BOMs, preventative maintenance plans, and documentation for internal builds and external vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with manufacturing engineers to define and capture process requirements into robust, operator-friendly hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve assembly quality and throughput through fixture design, error-proofing, ergonomics, and process simplification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support build events and production launches by troubleshooting tooling and equipment issues directly on the floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive vendor builds from quote to fabrication, assembly, debug, installation, and acceptance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and refine tooling for operations such as alignment, joining, fastening, pressing, dispensing, inspection, and functional test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize tooling designs and components where possible to reduce cost, lead time, and maintenance burden.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience designing manufacturing equipment, tooling, or fixtures in a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mechanical design skills, including GD&amp;amp;T, tolerance stack-up, mechanism design, and material/process selection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in 3D CAD; Siemens NX preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and releasing custom tooling for repeatable assembly of electro-mechanical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience supporting fabrication, build, debug, and commissioning of production equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with common factory hardware such as pneumatics, sensors, actuators, linear motion, and machine guarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of DFM/DFA, ergonomics, poka-yoke, and operator-centered tooling design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with design, quality, technicians, and vendors in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment, ownership, and willingness to spend time on the manufacturing floor solving problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Else You Need to Know&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting cash range for this role is Salary range: $125,000 - $170,000.00. Please note that this is a target, starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. We are always open to negotiation. The final cash pay for this role will depend on a variety of factors, including a specific candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may also include: equity compensation; discretionary annual or performance bonuses; sales incentives; benefits such as medical, dental and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws or our own sensibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’d like to learn more about Zipline and our teams, feel free to check out our Instagram, one of our Reddit AMA’s, or our website!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

a16z-zipline:greenhouse:7780020003.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You and The Role&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is seeking a Senior Recruiting Partner to help support the growth of our non technical teams.&amp;nbsp; We are pioneering autonomous logistics at a global scale, and our technology is fundamentally rewriting how the world moves critical goods. To support this massive expansion, we are seeking an exceptional Senior Recruiting Partner to help build the world-class teams that will define our next stage of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a high-impact opportunity to act as a talent architect across our most critical non technical functions—specifically anchoring searches across G&amp;amp;A (Finance, Legal, People, Workplace), Operations, and Sales / Go-To-Market (GTM).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a business-as-usual recruiting role. We need someone who is genuinely energized by rapid scaling, leans into ambiguity, and views change as an opportunity to build something innovative and lasting. You will partner directly with hiring managers and executive leads to shape team capabilities, influence talent strategy, and deliver key hires that accelerate our business outcomes. The ideal candidate combines full-cycle recruiting expertise with strong business acumen, exceptional judgment, and a demonstrated track record of hiring revenue-generating, operational, and corporate talent in fast-paced, high-growth environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead full-cycle searches for top-tier talent across all levels of experience, including senior leadership roles, spanning our Operations, G&amp;amp;A (Finance, Legal, People), and Sales/GTM organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop proactive talent strategies to identify and attract top business, operational, and commercial professionals from highly competitive, fast-moving markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver exceptional candidate experiences while authentically representing Zipline’s mission, fast pace, and culture of customer obsession.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with hiring managers and business leaders as a trusted advisor to deeply understand Zipline&#39;s evolving operating model, commercial pipelines, and talent gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence hiring decisions through data, market intelligence, organizational insights, and structured talent assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help teams define hiring profiles that align with both immediate scaling needs and future organizational growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;section-wrapper page-full-width&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, with a proven track record of supporting a mix of Operations, G&amp;amp;A (Corporate/Administrative), and Sales/GTM roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success recruiting in hyper-growth, high-growth, or highly transformational companies where navigating rapid change is the norm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering directly with hiring managers and business stakeholders to align on talent strategies and headcount planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of independently leading candidate searches from initial strategy through to a successful close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in creative sourcing, talent mapping, candidate assessment, and high-touch candidate management for diverse business functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication with an ability to simplify complex ideas and move with urgency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;content-wrapper posting-page&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with complex B2B commercial structures, enterprise pipeline dynamics, or multi-stakeholder enterprise sales cycles (e.g., selling into major healthcare systems, logistics, e-commerce, or retail giants).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with the ability to create, measure, and scale hiring workflows between candidates, hiring managers, and the recruiting team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting within a fast-moving startup environment where scaling structures require high adaptability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Greenhouse, GEM, Goodtime, Google Suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;content-wrapper posting-page&quot;&gt;What Else You Need to Know&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting cash range for this role is $120,000 - $180,000. Please note that this is a target, starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. The final cash pay for this role will depend on a variety of factors, including a specific candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may also include: equity compensation; discretionary annual or performance bonuses; sales incentives; benefits such as medical, dental and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to&amp;nbsp;race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion or religious creed, mental or physical disability, medical condition, genetic information, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, military or veteran status, citizenship, or other characteristics protected by state, federal or local law or our other policies.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

adventinternational-zenoti:greenhouse:77.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Zenoti provides an all-in-one, cloud-based software solution for the beauty and wellness industry. Our solution allows users to seamlessly manage every aspect of the business in a comprehensive mobile solution: online appointment bookings, POS, CRM, employee management, inventory management, built-in marketing programs and more. Zenoti helps clients streamline their systems and reduce costs, while simultaneously improving customer retention and spending. Our platform is engineered for reliability and scale and harnesses the power of enterprise-level technology for businesses of all sizes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zenoti powers more than 30,000 salons, spas, medspas and fitness studios in over 50 countries. This includes a vast portfolio of global brands, such as European Wax Center, Hand &amp;amp; Stone, Massage Heights, Rush Hair &amp;amp; Beauty, Sono Bello, Profile by Sanford, Hair Cuttery, CorePower Yoga and TONI&amp;amp;GUY.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our recent accomplishments include surpassing a $1 billion unicorn valuation, being named Next Tech Titan by GeekWire, raising an $80 million investment from TPG, ranking as the 316th fastest-growing company in North America on Deloitte’s 2020 Technology Fast 500™. We are also proud to be recognized as a Great Place to Work CertifiedTM for 2021-2022 as this reaffirms our commitment to empowering people to feel good and find their greatness. To learn more about Zenoti visit: https://www.zenoti.com&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-redactor-tag=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;What&#39;s the opportunity?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customer Success Manager (CSM) is ultimately responsible for ensuring the success of the portfolio of Zenoti’s customers. The CSM will bring Zenoti’s best ideas, innovations, and capabilities to their portfolio of customers and match these to the customers’ business goals, driving greater business value and executive alignment between Zenoti and the Customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-redactor-tag=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;What will I be doing ?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating value, revenue, results and rock-solid relationships with Zenoti customers by being a strategic, trusted business partner and advocate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyzing and gaining insight into the customer’s business, market, industry, and revenue model, and then driving recommendations and solutions leveraging Zenoti capabilities to deliver revenue and results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consulting with existing and new customers to ensure they are getting the most out of the Zenoti system, and where required, engaging with relevant team members across the organization to ensure challenges faced are addressed in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing a solid understanding of the customer&#39;s technical environment and business goals, to inform and develop a long-term account solution strategy and road-map, working in tandem with the product team.\&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying, developing and maintaining strong relationships with stakeholders at all necessary levels (C-suite, management and functional) within the customer organization to understand and influence their project strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive periodic customer engagements and touch-points to inform “Customer Health”, manage expectations, identify necessary escalations and ensure continued high customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-redactor-tag=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;What skills do I need?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked with large scale enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to work in a competitive environment where one’s growth potential is driven by one’s abilities and attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with and/or an understanding of the wellness industry is strongly recommended&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing SaaS or Cloud technical accounts with desire to learn new value propositions, products, and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous Senior-level Program Management or Product Management experience a huge plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in customer-facing project/engagement management, technical pre-sales or other enterprise software IT/technical delivery or consulting role (Professional Services or Software Licensing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze a business in the wellness industry, both qualitatively and quantitatively, and articulate challenges, opportunities, and solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive facilitator, with excellent presentation and written communication skills working with C-Suite/VPs/Directors to understand needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for customer success, driven by customer satisfaction, product adoption, and achieving revenue results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-year Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Business or any relevant discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 or more years of strong relevant experience in customer facing technology customer success or sales role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Zenoti, we believe that when people feel good, they are able to do great things. We enable our employees to unleash their potential by providing enriching career opportunities and dynamic financial rewards. We foster an enriching culture and encourage our employees to balance life, work, and wellbeing. We offer all of our employees:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A competitive base salary, plus commission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligibility to receive equity through company Employee Stock Option Plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programs, classes and activities supporting your physical and mental well being, led by Zenoti&#39;s dedicated Chief Wellness Officer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Zenoti provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation and training.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

allegiscyber-dragos:greenhouse:521247900.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dragos is on a relentless mission to defend industrial organizations that provide us with the necessities of modern civilization; running water, functioning electricity, and safe industrial working environments. As the market leader in ICS/OT Cybersecurity, we are dedicated to arming our customers with best-in-class technology, threat intelligence, and services to protect their systems as effectively and efficiently as possible. We’re a remote-first culture with operations in North America, Europe, the Middle East, and APAC. We’re looking for mission-oriented teammates who embody our core values of authenticity, transparency, and trust. Are you ready to make a difference? Come join a mission that can save the world!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;Our Customer Experience team is seeking a Resident Engineer who will partner with one of our customers in Houston. In this role, you will serve as an onsite, customer-facing technical expert responsible for planning, deploying, and optimizing the Dragos Platform within the customer&#39;s industrial environment. You will work hands-on at customer facilities to install the platform, tune it to their operational needs, and ensure reliable security coverage across their ICS/OT systems. Serving as a trusted technical partner, you&#39;ll guide customers through deployment, troubleshooting, and ongoing platform adoption, enabling them to strengthen and sustain the security of their critical infrastructure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Collaborate with Dragos Sales and Solution Architect teams to understand customer use cases, success criteria, and define Dragos Platform objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Partner with client teams on network architecture, sensor placement, and integrations; coordinate and conduct full deployments including upgrades, patches, and configuration changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Tune, optimize, and monitor the Dragos Platform to meet defined customer objectives and ensure continuous availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Develop content, build foundational workflows, and provide troubleshooting and break/fix support; manage escalations as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Provide knowledge transfer, training, and new release feature walkthroughs to key stakeholders while documenting processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Maintain ongoing client engagement by soliciting feedback on feature requests, communicating product roadmap updates, and identifying opportunities for additional Dragos products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Coordinate and collaborate with internal Dragos teams including Intel and Threat Hunting to deliver comprehensive customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must live within a reasonable commuting distance of Houston, TX and be willing to work a hybrid schedule that includes regular onsite work at customer facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;5+ years of ICS/OT cybersecurity experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Networking experience including strong knowledge of IP networks, OSI model, Purdue model, and ICS protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Experience with Linux (command line), Docker, scripting languages (Python, shell, etc.), SIEMs, and ELK stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Experience with on-premise and cloud software solutions for the enterprise, with the ability to manage multiple stakeholders and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Customer-oriented and attentive to client needs, with strong interpersonal and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Willingness to travel up to 25%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Compensation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;3&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559683&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559684&amp;quot;:-2,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Salary: $155,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;3&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559683&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559684&amp;quot;:-2,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Competitive Equity Package &lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;3&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559683&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559684&amp;quot;:-2,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Comprehensive Benefits Plan&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;#LI-JF1 #LI-REMOTE&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dragos is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, orientation, national origin, age, disability, genetics, or any other basis forbidden under federal, state, or local laws. All new hires must pass a background check as a condition of employment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

alphapartners-coupang:greenhouse:7809745.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Safety Manager&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Description&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Safety &amp;amp; Compliance Management &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Safety &amp;amp; Compliance Management Develop, implement, and enforce fire safety policies and procedures in compliance with Taiwan&#39;s fire codes and regulations. Conduct fire risk assessments, safety inspections, and audits to identify potential hazards and recommend mitigation strategies. Collaborate with regulatory agencies, authorities having jurisdiction (AHJs), and fire departments to ensure compliance with fire safety laws. Lead fire protection system inspections, maintenance, and performance evaluations to ensure optimal functionality.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Prevention &amp;amp; Risk Mitigation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Prevention &amp;amp; Risk Mitigation Establish and execute fire prevention programs, ensuring best practices are adopted across all facilities. Oversee the design, installation, and maintenance of fire detection, alarm, and suppression systems. Implement hot work permit programs, fire drills, and evacuation plans to ensure operational readiness. Develop and maintain fire load assessments to evaluate and minimize potential fire risks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Emergency Response &amp;amp; Crisis Management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Emergency Response &amp;amp; Crisis Management Lead the development of fire emergency response plans and conduct regular fire drills. Train employees and emergency response teams on fire safety procedures, evacuation protocols, and fire extinguisher use. Act as a liaison with local emergency services to coordinate emergency response efforts effectively. Develop business continuity strategies related to fire incidents to minimize disruptions and ensure swift recovery.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Safety Training &amp;amp; Awareness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Safety Training &amp;amp; Awareness Design and deliver fire safety training programs for employees, contractors, and facility teams. Ensure all personnel are equipped with knowledge of fire prevention and practices and emergency response protocols. Foster a strong fire safety culture through awareness campaigns and engagement initiatives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Data Management &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Data Management &amp;amp; Reporting Maintain comprehensive records of fire incidents, safety inspections, and compliance reports. Analyze fire safety data to identify trends and drive continuous improvement initiatives. Provide executive-level reports and recommendations on fire safety performance and risk reduction strategies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Qualifications Required: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Fire Safety, Fire Science, Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Minimum of 8 years of fire prevention experience, preferably in a corporate, industrial, or authority having jurisdiction (AHJ) setting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Strong knowledge of Taiwan&#39;s fire safety regulations, NFPA standards, and global fire codes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience in fire risk assessment, compliance audits, and emergency planning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Proficiency in fire protection system design, maintenance, and evaluation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Excellent leadership, problem solving, and stakeholder management skills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Preferred: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Advanced degree in Fire Science, Engineering or Occupational Safety.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Certifications such as Certified Fire Protection Specialist (CFPS), NFPA, or equivalent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience with fire safety technology, AI-enabled fire monitoring, and digital compliance tracking.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Bilingual proficiency in Mandarin and English.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Prior experience in multinational corporations or high-risk operational environments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;31&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;multilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Your personal information will be collected and managed by Coupang as stated in the Application Privacy Notice located below:&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coupang.jobs/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;https://www.coupang.jobs/privacy-policy/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

alphapartners-coupang:greenhouse:7864690.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Introduction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We exist to wow our customers. We know we’re doing the right thing when we hear our customers say, “How did we ever live without Coupang?” Born out of an obsession to make shopping, eating, and living easier than ever, we’re collectively disrupting the multi-billion-dollar e-commerce industry from the ground up. We are one of the fastest-growing e-commerce companies that established an unparalleled reputation for being a dominant and reliable force in South Korean commerce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to have the best of both worlds — a startup culture with the resources of a large global public company. This fuels us to continue our growth and launch new services at the speed we have been since our inception. We are all entrepreneurs surrounded by opportunities to drive new initiatives and innovations. At our core, we are bold and ambitious people that like to get our hands dirty and make a hands-on impact. At Coupang, you will see yourself, your colleagues, your team, and the company grow every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission to build the future of commerce is real. We push the boundaries of what’s possible to solve problems and break traditional tradeoffs. Join Coupang now to create an epic experience in this always-on, high-tech, and hyper-connected world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Manager for the Coupang Pricing Team, you will be responsible for developing scalable pricing solutions for our business stakeholders across millions of catalog items and competitor pricing data points. You will collaborate with leaders from engineering, data science, operations, and various business teams to help protect Coupang customer trust in our prices and drive opportunities for future business growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product vision, strategy, roadmap, and KPIs for one or more areas within pricing system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the entire product lifecycle, from ideation to launch, including defining product requirements, identifying use cases, and establishing success metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify new opportunities to enhance key business metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new product development with clear objectives and timelines, fostering collaboration across teams and employing rigorous project management methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire the team with your product vision, collaborating cross-functionally to realize it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of product management experience, with a track record of developing and executing a compelling product vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous e-commerce or pricing domain experience preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership experience with a history of successfully launching and sustaining products and programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An analytical mindset suited to a fast-paced, data-driven, highly dynamic start-up like environment and the capability to translate ambiguous problems into insights, scoped features, and projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and the ability to communicate effectively and influence others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, enabling effective interaction with both technical and business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to understand technical challenges and make educated trade-offs between time, resources, and business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of mentoring and developing more junior team members into future company leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias for action and a willingness to roll up your sleeves to get things done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master degree in a quantitative field (business, engineering, statistics) or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in international environments and globally distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience tackling ambiguous business and operational challenges, including the ability to model decision problems effectively, at the right level of abstraction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in international environments and globally distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in both English and Mandarin preferred, but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Review -&amp;gt; Phone Interview -&amp;gt; Onsite (or Virtual Onsite) Interview –&amp;gt; Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The exact nature of the recruitment process may vary according to the specific job and may be changed due to scheduling or other circumstances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview schedules and the results will be informed to the applicant via the e-mail address submitted at the application stage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Details to Consider&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is open to Singapore Citizens and Permanent Residents only&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This job posting may be closed prior to the stated end date for application if all openings are filled.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coupang has the right to rescind an offer of employment if a candidate is found to have submitted false information as part of the application process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Those eligible for employment protection (recipients of veteran’s benefits, the disabled, etc.) may receive preferential treatment for employment in accordance with applicable laws.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Job titles and responsibilities may be subject to change depending on the candidate’s overall experience, etc. This will be communicated to the candidate at the appropriate time before the offer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring may be restricted in case the legal qualifications required for hiring and work performance is not met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your personal information will be collected and managed by Coupang as stated in the Application Privacy Notice located below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://privacy.coupang.com/en/land/jobs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://privacy.coupang.com/en/land/jobs/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

