&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Platform Product Manager,&amp;nbsp; Cloud Security Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Palo Alto, CA (also open to other locations)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Staff Product Manager for Cloud Security Architecture is a strategic role responsible for ensuring that Rubrik&#39;s cloud product offerings meet enterprise expectations for security and are secured from cyber-attacks. This technical role combines deep security expertise with strong product instincts and competitor awareness to translate customers&#39; security challenges and concerns into actionable product requirements for Rubrik’s cloud product and cloud platform security roadmap.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our product stands on a foundation of &quot;Zero Trust&quot; security and this role is critical in driving the long-term security vision and roadmap with a&amp;nbsp; focus on identifying product gaps, market opportunities, developing long-term strategic plans, and implementing enhancements that drive industry-leading security standards and best practices into Rubrik products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Specific Responsibilities:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works closely with cloud product and engineering teams to develop a deep understanding of the Rubrik cloud product architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to articulate and defend our architectural decisions cross functionally and to customers.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to cloud product and cloud platform&amp;nbsp; security roadmap and execute for multiple, related security domains within the Rubrik offering, ensuring alignment and coherence across the portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scan and keep abreast ofcustomer expectations and evolving hyperscaler best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a primary evangelist for the cloud product security and work with customers and account teams to define and evolve the roadmap across multiple dimensions (UX, technology, business) and deliver commercially viable security features and integrations across the Rubrik cloud portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional strategic initiatives and manage the execution across all cloud products, ensuring they meet platform security standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop product risk identification, assessment, and resolution prioritization for high-impact platform vulnerabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with and influence senior cross-functional stakeholders—including InfoSec, Engineering, User Experience, Sales, Marketing, Operations, and Support—to align vision across business units and secure project approval and resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate concisely and clearly to diverse audiences, including presenting compelling business cases to executive leadership and representing Rubrik as a security expert to external audiences, customers, and ecosystem partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive significant business impact by identifying market opportunities and leading new product developments that contribute measurable increases to quarterly revenue, profitability, and customer trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a mentor and role model for other Product Managers, sharing best practices, driving clarity in the face of ambiguity cross-functionally, and fostering strong partnerships with engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Required Skills:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience or desire to be in Product Management, with at least 3 years focused on enterprise cloud product development with hyperscalers, ideally in a hands-on technical or architecture role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience as a Security Architect, Solutions Architect, or Senior/Staff Engineer is highly desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in cloud security and threat modeling and working knowledge of big 3 hyperscalers with specific experience in cloud security posture management or secure cloud integration and defining secure architectures for solutions built on hyperscaler infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with API security, microservices architecture, and container security (e.g., Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in owning and managing the strategy and execution of multiple, high-impact products simultaneously, leveraging a deep understanding of the underlying technology stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to define, scope, and deliver large, complex features, leveraging deep technical acumen to define architecture, requirements, and measurable KPIs/goals while engaging effectively with cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to clearly articulate complex technical concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the following security domains:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zero Trust architecture and security principles, including experience translating those principles into product requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authentication and authorization (SSO, SAML, OpenID, RBAC), for both human and non-human (API) actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data protection, immutable storage, and encryption technologies, including understanding of cryptographic primitives and key management architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in a technical field (e.g., Computer Science, Engineering) or equivalent work experience; advanced degree and/or relevant cybersecurity certifications (e.g., CCSP, CISSP, CCSK) highly desired.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The minimum and maximum base salaries for this role are posted below; additionally, the role is eligible for bonus potential, equity and benefits. The range displayed reflects the minimum and maximum target for new hire salaries for the role based on U.S. location. Within the range, the salary offered will be determined by work location and additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$263,300 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join Us in Securing and Accelerating the World&#39;s AI Transformation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik (RBRK), the Security and AI Operations Company, leads at the intersection of data protection, cyber resilience, and enterprise AI acceleration. Rubrik Security Cloud delivers complete cyber resilience by securing, monitoring, and recovering data, identities, and workloads across clouds. Rubrik Agent Cloud accelerates trusted AI agent deployments at scale by monitoring and auditing agentic actions, enforcing real-time guardrails, fine-tuning for accuracy and undoing agentic mistakes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/rubrik-inc/mycompany/verification/&quot;&gt;Linkedin&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/rubrikinc&quot;&gt;X (formerly Twitter)&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/rubrikinc/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.rubrik.com&quot;&gt;Rubrik.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Inclusion @ Rubrik&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Rubrik, we are dedicated to fostering a culture where people from all backgrounds are valued, feel they belong, and believe they can succeed. Our commitment to inclusion is at the heart of our mission to secure the world’s data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to hire and promote the best talent, regardless of background. We continually review our hiring practices to ensure fairness and strive to create an environment where every employee has equal access to opportunities for growth and excellence. We believe in empowering everyone to bring their authentic selves to work and achieve their fullest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our inclusion strategy focuses on three core areas of our business and culture:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Our Company: We are committed to building a merit-based organization that offers equal access to growth and success for all employees globally. Your potential is limitless here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Culture: We strive to create an inclusive atmosphere where individuals from all backgrounds feel a strong sense of belonging, can thrive, and do their best work. Your contributions help us innovate and break boundaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Our Communities: We are dedicated to expanding our engagement with the communities we operate in, creating opportunities for underrepresented talent and driving greater innovation for our clients. Your impact extends beyond Rubrik, contributing to safer and stronger communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, or protected veteran status and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability or genetics. In addition to federal law requirements, Rubrik complies with applicable state and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment in every location in which the company has facilities. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation and training.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please contact us at hr@rubrik.com if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process or work procedures, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO IS THE LAW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/olms/regs/compliance/eo_posters/employeerightsposter2page_19final.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;NOTIFICATION OF EMPLOYEE RIGHTS UNDER FEDERAL LABOR LAWS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

